  "notes": [
    "Bitcoin Core has no MAINTAINERS file in-tree; GitHub collaborators API requires push access.",
    "This list is the project canonical set used for enrichment and analyses (merge-authority / historical maintainers).",
    "Roster membership is not merge keys. Only observed GitHub merged_by logins can merge. See merge_capability.json.",
    "Everyone else cannot merge: a zero as merger is lack of keys, not unused privilege. Reviewer/ACK is not merge authority.",
    "Non-maintainer 'merge rate' means a key holder merged their PR (author-success), never that they merged.",
    "Timeline periods are inferred from merged_by activity and layered on top of this set.",
    "email_aliases / name_aliases / nick_aliases collapse documented same-person variants at analysis time. Do not rewrite raw corpora.",
    "TheCharlatan and sedited stay distinct GitHub logins (account rename). They are one human; merge them only in informal nick joins, not in the maintainer login set."
